  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinCare 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "Halfway through a trial, your brother begins to feel discouraged because
    the side effects are challenging, and treatment results aren\u2019t yet clear.
    You reassure him that participation is always voluntary, and he can leave the
    trial at any time for any reason.\n\n<b>In this situation, what key responsibility
    is the caregiver demonstrating?</b>"
  explanation: "Caregivers help patients understand their rights, including informed
    consent and the option to withdraw at any time, serving as advocates for patient
    autonomy and well-being throughout the trial process. By making sure patients
    never feel pressured or confused about their choices, caregivers reinforce the
    ethical foundation of clinical research, ensuring that participation remains
    voluntary, respectful, and centered on the patient\u2019s best interests."
  correctAnswer: Reminding the patient of their rights during a clinical trial
  incorrectAnswer1: Helping the patient stay on track with their treatment plan
  incorrectAnswer2: Sharing important trial information with the research team
  incorrectAnswer3: Observing and sharing how the patient is responding to treatment
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Clinical
